+
+## Installed terminal command
+
+The qualified package also exposes `household-record`. Install the prepared
+package into an explicit local prefix using your existing Node/npm runtime:
+
+```sh
+npm install --ignore-scripts --prefix ./household-local ./household-ledger-mcp-0.1.0.tgz
+./household-local/node_modules/.bin/household-record --help
+./household-local/node_modules/.bin/household-record new --endpoint http://127.0.0.1:3000/mcp --request /NEW/private/request.json
+./household-local/node_modules/.bin/household-record resume --request /existing/private/request.json
+```
+
+On Windows, invoke the generated `household-record.cmd` in that same `.bin`
+directory. The native POSIX installation is qualified separately from the
+unchanged direct-path command; Windows installed execution requires its own
+receiving. These commands do not start a server or add a global PATH entry.
+Use the same already-running, loopback-only service and ledger for a saved
+request and its explicit retry. Reinstalling the command does not migrate data.
+The realpath guard also permits an explicitly created local link to the installed
+command while passive module imports stay inactive.
